<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Odo II of Blois</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">985–<a href="/years/1037">1037</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Odo II, Count of Blois</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Odo II was count of Blois, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chartres">Chartres</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tours">Tours</a> from 1004 and one of the most powerful French nobles of his day. Around 1022 he acquired <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/troyes">Troyes</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meaux">Meaux</a>, the core of the later county of Champagne, surrounding the royal lands. He claimed the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> and was killed in 1037 at the Battle of Bar while fighting the emperor's supporters.</p></div>
